{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cep88AXKzwhherNqLHsbf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The implementation is complete and all acceptance criteria are met:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the shipment confirmation endpoint (`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`) with the following changes:\n\n**Changes made:**\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added the `confirm` endpoint that:\n   - Moves shipments from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED` status\n   - Handles idempotent retries (already `CONFIRMED` shipments succeed without change)\n   - Rejects `CANCELLED` shipments with HTTP 409\n   - Returns 404 for non-existent shipments\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** - Added `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` error code for shipment state conflicts\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 4 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Confirming a created shipment\n   - Idempotency of the confirm operation\n   - Rejection of cancelled shipments (409)\n   - Rejection of non-existent shipments (404)\n\n**Test results:** All 17 tests pass (5 original + 4 new shipment tests + 8 other tests)\n\nThe implementation preserves the existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture, uses no new dependencies, and follows the established error handling patterns in the API."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":643,"cache_read_input_tokens":42816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":643},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7168188d-c27a-4647-ba0a-13a739d9c726","uuid":"fc3a7a3b-4aa4-46b3-8874-be356a56d203","timestamp":"2026-09-07T13:02:25.206Z","request_id":"req_011Cep889pf6tPw4HYhMvUb5"}
